{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["The sense of <b>for it is a stiff-necked people</b> is according to its plain meaning: that He should go among them because they are a stiff-necked people. For after HaKadosh Baruch Hu has been reconciled to them, it is better for their stiff necks that YHWH Himself go rather than an angel, and He seeks to increase their good all the more, for they are His people and His inheritance. And just as at the time of anger it was better for them that He send an angel before them because they are a stiff-necked people, as He said (Exodus 33:3), \"lest I consume you,\" so at the time of favor it is better for them with the Shekhinah because they are a stiff-necked people, for He will show all the more grace and compassion upon His servants. And HaShem answered him that He would do so — that He would cut the covenant and perform wonders through him, as he asked: \"and I and Your people will be distinguished\" (above 33:16).\n\nAnd he said <b>in the sight of all Your people</b>, <b>and let all the people see that You are among them</b> — for these great and awesome deeds He will perform with Moses and on his account, and the people will be in the covenant. And it is not reasonable to interpret that He promises to perform now for Israel wonders such as have never been created before in all the earth and among all the nations, for no greater wonders were done for them after this than what was done with them at the beginning in Egypt and at the Sea; rather, greater things were created and done with them at the outset. But the matter alludes to the dwelling of the Shekhinah among them, and to His being with Moses for honor and splendor, in the hidden and in the wondrous, as He said (ibid.), \"and we will be distinguished,\" as I explained (above 33:14–16, s.v. אבל). May HaKadosh Baruch Hu show us wonders from His Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The phrase והשם ענהו appears to refer to God's response to Moses; rendered HaShem. The final line is a standard pious closing formula."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:22.731845842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}